{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_adr", "label": "ADR 0003: the control plane is a Unix socket, not localhost TCP", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/adr/0003-unix-socket-control-plane.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Status accepted. Chooses among the sketch's options (localhost HTTP, Unix domain socket, named pipe, platform IPC) on the grounds that the control plane is the door to every workspace secret."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_control_plane", "label": "Local runtime control plane", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0003-unix-socket-control-plane.md", "source_location": "lines 14-15", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Anything that can reach it can publish to any channel, call any peer, read runtime status and add exposures. The capability behind the listener, not the listener's transport, is the threat."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_unix_domain_socket", "label": "Unix domain socket at mode 0600", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0003-unix-socket-control-plane.md", "source_location": "lines 11, 19", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A socket file is governed by filesystem permissions the OS already enforces and operators already understand; 0600 in the runtime's data directory means the owner and nobody else, and permissions are visible with ls -l."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_named_pipe_windows", "label": "Named pipe on Windows", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0003-unix-socket-control-plane.md", "source_location": "lines 11, 25", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Windows has no Unix socket, so path handling carries a platform branch. That branch is the accepted cost of never using TCP."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_localhost_tcp_rejected", "label": "Localhost TCP control plane (rejected)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0003-unix-socket-control-plane.md", "source_location": "lines 11, 17", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A 127.0.0.1 port is reachable by every process running as any user on the machine, by every container sharing the network namespace, and with a misconfigured Docker port publish or a 0.0.0.0 bind from outside."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_token_scheme_rejected", "label": "Token authentication scheme (rejected)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0003-unix-socket-control-plane.md", "source_location": "lines 17, 23", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No authentication step fixes a TCP control plane without inventing a token scheme, storing that token somewhere, and having every client find it. Avoiding it means nothing to design, distribute or leak."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_filesystem_permissions", "label": "Filesystem permissions as the access control mechanism", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0003-unix-socket-control-plane.md", "source_location": "line 19", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reuse of an enforcement mechanism the operating system already provides and operators already read, instead of a bespoke authentication layer."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_container_isolation_cost", "label": "Cross-container clients must mount the socket", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0003-unix-socket-control-plane.md", "source_location": "line 25", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A client in a different container cannot reach the runtime without mounting the socket, which is deliberate rather than an oversight."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_optin_networked_listener", "label": "Future opt-in networked listener", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0003-unix-socket-control-plane.md", "source_location": "line 27", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If a networked control plane is ever genuinely needed it must be a separate opt-in listener with real authentication, never a relaxation of the socket decision."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_adr", "target": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_unix_domain_socket", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0003-unix-socket-control-plane.md", "source_location": "line 11", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_adr", "target": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_named_pipe_windows", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0003-unix-socket-control-plane.md", "source_location": "line 11", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_adr", "target": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_localhost_tcp_rejected", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0003-unix-socket-control-plane.md", "source_location": "lines 11, 17", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_control_plane", "target": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_adr", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0003-unix-socket-control-plane.md", "source_location": "line 15", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_unix_domain_socket", "target": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_filesystem_permissions", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0003-unix-socket-control-plane.md", "source_location": "line 19", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_filesystem_permissions", "target": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_token_scheme_rejected", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0003-unix-socket-control-plane.md", "source_location": "lines 17-23", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_localhost_tcp_rejected", "target": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_token_scheme_rejected", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0003-unix-socket-control-plane.md", "source_location": "line 17", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_named_pipe_windows", "target": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_unix_domain_socket", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/adr/0003-unix-socket-control-plane.md", "source_location": "lines 11, 25", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_container_isolation_cost", "target": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_unix_domain_socket", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0003-unix-socket-control-plane.md", "source_location": "line 25", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_optin_networked_listener", "target": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_adr", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0003-unix-socket-control-plane.md", "source_location": "line 27", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_optin_networked_listener", "target": "docs_a